Splunk Commands and Concepts Learned
- index: Specifies the index containing the events.
- sourcetype: Filters data according to its source type or format.
- index=main: Search for all events stored in the main index.
- timechart: Creates time-based statistical charts.
- count: Counts matching events.
- stats: Calculates statistics from search results.
- top: Identifies the most frequently occurring values in a specified field.
- rare: Identifies the least frequently occurring values in a specified field.
- vertical bar (|) : Passes results from one search command to another.

Basic Searches
- sourcetype="vendor_sales/vendor_sales"
- sourcetype="www1/secure"
- sourcetype="access_combined_wcookie"
- sourcetype="access_combined_wcookie" status !=200 | timechart count
- sourcetype="access_combined_wcookie" status !=200 | stats count by categoryId
- sourcetype="access_combined_wcookie" | table clientip action status| rename clientip as "Host Address", action as "Customer Action"
- sourcetype="access_combined_wcookie" | table clientip action status| dedup status| sort -status
- sourcetype="vendor_sales/vendor_sales" Code = D OR Code = E | top VendorID
- index=main | rare limit=5 useragent
